      "content": "Understood. So the burden of proof is really on the tenant to show it wasn't a predictable risk. To push this a bit further, if the tenant tries to argue that the regulatory change was an \"act of chaos\" or something similarly unpredictable that essentially disrupted the very foundation of the contract, how would a court view that kind of reasoning? Do they even consider the \"unpredictability\" of the event as a matter of principle, or is it strictly tied to the written text of the clause?",
